The negative examples quoted in the new bullets are not hypothetical;
they are lifted from notes this skill produced for a whitespace
series in CervEdin/git-test earlier today. There is a risk in
quoting them: vivid negative examples sit in the context window and
can prime the register they ban. I kept them anyway because naming
the exact moves is what steers a model off them, and kept the
wording terse to limit the exposure.

I considered a dedicated section ("Restraint" / "The AI failure
mode") and rejected it. A section narrating model behavior is itself
the wrong register, and instruction text doubles as example text, so
the rules were folded into existing sections and written dry.

The deletion pass went into step 3 rather than a new numbered step
to avoid renumbering. It may be partly redundant with the new
bullets in PEFF-STYLE.md; my guess is a process step holds better
over a long generation than a one-time prohibition, but I have not
measured that.

peff-review, sunshine-review, and gitster-review likely have the
same vocabulary-prescribing tone sections; this commit does not
touch them.
